## Reflection

This was my first Verilog project, and it helped me understand how hardware description languages differ from traditional programming languages.
I learned how to define a module, declare inputs and outputs, and use the'assign' statement to describe combinational logic. I also learnt how to verify the design using GTKwave.
This project gave me a good foundation for more complex cobinational circuits, such as multiplexers and decoders.

## Problems

I had troubles with using GTKwave since it required me to convert my .v-file into a .vvp-file. I also had troubles re-writing my code to work with GTKwave.
It was hard to swap from the traditional programming mindset into a HDL mindset. So I often mixed up concepts.

